<section class="sec" id="features"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="center r">
    <div class="eyebrow">What you get</div>
    <h2 class="sech">Your whole collection,<br/>release-accurate.</h2>
    <p>Bring the albums you already own into one good-looking library, and take it everywhere you go.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cards">
    <div class="fcard r">
      <div class="top">
        <div class="emoji" style="background:rgba(155,108,246,.18);color:var(--violet)"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 20h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-7.9a2 2 0 0 1-1.69-.9L9.6 3.9A2 2 0 0 0 7.93 3H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v13a2 2 0 0 0 2 2z"/><path d="M12 10v6m-2.5-2.5L12 16l2.5-2.5"/></svg></div>
        <span class="no">01</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Releases, not files</h3>
      <p>bae understands your music as releases, not a folder of loose files. Point it at what you already own, ripped CDs, purchased downloads, Bandcamp buys, and bae matches each to the right release for accurate track names, cover art, and credits, and keeps the different releases of an album together as one.</p>
      <div class="tags"><span>MusicBrainz &amp; Discogs</span><span>Cover art</span><span>Releases grouped</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="fcard r d1">
      <div class="top">
        <div class="emoji" style="background:rgba(134,224,200,.18);color:var(--mint)"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 12a9 9 0 0 1 15-6.7L21 8"/><path d="M21 3v5h-5"/><path d="M21 12a9 9 0 0 1-15 6.7L3 16"/><path d="M3 21v-5h5"/></svg></div>
        <span class="no">02</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Bigger than any one device</h3>
      <p>Your whole collection lives in your cloud home, so every device shows all of it, even a phone too small to hold it. Tracks download as you play, and anything you pin stays on the device for offline.</p>
      <div class="tags"><span>Desktop &amp; phone</span><span>Whole library, any device</span><span>Pin for offline</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="fcard r">
      <div class="top">
        <div class="emoji" style="background:rgba(247,168,196,.2);color:var(--pink-deep)"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/></svg></div>
        <span class="no">03</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Sounds the way it should</h3>
      <p>Whole albums play start to finish the way the artist meant them, gapless, with FLAC, CUE sheets, and vinyl side breaks all handled right.</p>
      <div class="tags"><span>FLAC &amp; CUE</span><span>Gapless</span><span>Vinyl side breaks</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="fcard r d1">
      <div class="top">
        <div class="emoji" style="background:rgba(155,108,246,.18);color:var(--violet)"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17.5 19a4.5 4.5 0 1 0-1.4-8.8A6 6 0 1 0 6 16h11.5z"/></svg></div>
        <span class="no">04</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Yours for good</h3>
      <p>Your music stays in normal files that you control, keep them, move them, back them up. Nobody can take your collection away or change the deal.</p>
      <div class="tags"><span>You own the files</span><span>Yours to keep</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="sec" style="padding-top:0;"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="center r" style="margin-bottom:34px;">
    <div class="eyebrow">Good to know</div>
    <h2 class="sech">A few things you'll care about.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="minigrid">
    <div class="mini r">
      <div class="mico" style="background:rgba(134,224,200,.18);color:var(--mint)"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17.8 19.2 16 11l3.5-3.5C21 6 21.5 4 21 3c-1-.5-3 0-4.5 1.5L13 8 4.8 6.2c-.5-.1-.9.1-1.1.5l-.3.5c-.2.5-.1 1 .3 1.3L9 12l-2 3H4l-1 1 3 2 2 3 1-1v-3l3-2 3.5 5.3c.3.4.8.5 1.3.3l.5-.2c.4-.3.6-.7.5-1.2z"/></svg></div>
      <h4>Plays offline</h4>
      <p>Play an album once or pin it and it's saved to your device. Lose signal or hop on a plane and your downloaded music keeps playing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mini r d1">
      <div class="mico" style="background:rgba(155,108,246,.18);color:var(--violet)"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 10v3"/><path d="M6 6v11"/><path d="M10 3v18"/><path d="M14 8v7"/><path d="M18 5v13"/><path d="M22 10v3"/></svg></div>
      <h4>Original quality</h4>
      <p>No re-encoding, ever. Your files stay exactly as they are, and you listen at that same original quality.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mini r d2">
      <div class="mico" style="background:rgba(247,168,196,.2);color:var(--pink-deep)"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 20h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-7.9a2 2 0 0 1-1.69-.9L9.6 3.9A2 2 0 0 0 7.93 3H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v13a2 2 0 0 0 2 2z"/></svg></div>
      <h4>Use what you have</h4>
      <p>Point bae at your sorted-just-so collection and it catalogs everything in place, no moving or copying. Backing it up to the cloud is opt-in.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

